+# Tasks: S005 Delivery status
+
+**Input**: `spec.md` and `plan.md` in this directory.
+
+**Prerequisites**: The supplied plan names a `delivery_events` migration, provider signature verification, an idempotent callback service, `POST /callbacks/reminder`, and `GET /actions/{id}/delivery`. No application tree, schema conventions, contract files, or test command are supplied in this workspace.
+
+**Reversible layout assumption**: Until the implementation repository establishes its own convention, use `migrations/`, `src/`, and `tests/integration/` at repository root. Rename these paths as one coherent mechanical move if the repository uses a different layout; do not change the behavior described below.
+
+## Implementation Context
+
+### Requirement → Task Mapping
+
+The source spec has one unnumbered SHALL. The following anchors split it without adding product scope.
+
+| Requirement | Requirement summary | Implementing tasks | Test coverage |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| R1 | Authenticate every provider callback before processing it. | 7, 9 | `tests/integration/test_reminder_callback.py` |
+| R2 | Deduplicate callbacks by provider event id. | 6, 8, 9 | `tests/integration/test_reminder_callback.py` |
+| R3 | Persist delivery status under the receiving workspace. | 6, 8 | `tests/integration/test_delivery_events_migration.py`, `tests/integration/test_reminder_callback.py` |
+| R4 | Expose an action’s delivery status only to its workspace. | 10 | `tests/integration/test_action_delivery.py` |
+
+### Design Decisions Carried from the Plan
+
+| Decision | Implementation consequence |
+|---|---|
+| `delivery_events` has workspace and provider-event uniqueness | The migration must enforce a workspace foreign-key relationship (where the existing schema provides one) and a unique provider-event id; application code must rely on the constraint for concurrent duplicate protection. |
+| Provider callback is authenticated | Reject a missing, malformed, or invalid signature before any event record is created or status is changed. |
+| Callback handling is idempotent | A duplicate provider event produces a successful non-duplicating result and must not repeat the status transition. |
+| Delivery reads are tenant scoped | The real request path must deny a caller from another workspace, rather than filtering only in a mocked service. |
+
+### Test Command Convention
+
+Each test task runs the repository’s integration-test command narrowed to its named file. The command must use the application’s request role and a real disposable database; a privileged/bypass role or mocked tenant policy is not acceptable evidence. The implementing agent records the concrete command in its implementation evidence once the repository’s runner is available.
