+## Phase 3: Implement persistence and callback handling
+
+- [ ] T005 Implement the `delivery_events` migration with the fields needed to identify the provider event, associated action, receiving workspace, delivery status, and timestamps; add the workspace relationship and provider-event uniqueness constraint; reconcile the migration head.
+
+**Implements**: R2, R3.
+
+**Pattern**: Use a forward-only migration that preserves existing data; uniqueness is the concurrency backstop for callback replays.
+
+**Acceptance predicate**: The migration probes pass for clean and dirty database shapes, and duplicate provider event insertion is rejected at the database boundary.
+
+**Test command**: Repository integration-test command narrowed to `tests/integration/test_delivery_events_migration.py`.
+
+**File**: `migrations/001_delivery_events.sql`
+
+- [ ] T006 Implement provider-signature verification that reads the configured provider secret through the repository’s existing configuration mechanism, verifies the raw callback payload and required signature header, and produces no persistence side effect on failure.
+
+**Implements**: R1.
+
+**Pattern**: Verify before parsing/dispatching status changes; keep secret material out of logs and responses.
+
+**Acceptance predicate**: Invalid signature cases in the callback integration test are rejected and leave no `delivery_events` row.
+
+**Test command**: Repository integration-test command narrowed to `tests/integration/test_reminder_callback.py`.
+
+**File**: `src/services/reminder_callback_auth.py`
